---
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { translations } from '../../../i18n/translations';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const t = translations[lang];
---
<LegalLayout
  lang={lang}
  currentRoute="terms"
  title={`${t.footer.terms} — Kaxa`}
  description={t.meta.description}
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="Last updated: July 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, installing, or using Kaxa ("the app", "the service") you agree to these Terms
    of Service. If you do not agree, you must not use the app. By downloading the app from Google
    Play or the App Store, you also agree to the terms of service of the corresponding store.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Description of the service</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa is a personal finance organization app that lets you track expenses and income, organize
    them into pockets, create budgets, track debts, and set savings goals. Kaxa includes an
    AI-assisted entry feature that processes text input to automatically categorize transactions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Kaxa is an organizational tool and does not constitute financial, legal, or tax
    advice.</strong> The AI feature may make interpretation or categorization errors; always
    verify automatically generated records before making financial decisions based on them.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Subscriptions and pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa offers the following subscription plans, managed through Google Play and/or the App
    Store via RevenueCat:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Weekly plan: $1.99 USD per week, with a 3-day free trial.</li>
    <li>Monthly plan: $4.99 USD per month.</li>
    <li>Yearly plan: $24.99 USD per year (best value).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Prices may vary based on local taxes applied by the app store.
    <strong>Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each period</strong> unless cancelled
    before the renewal date from your Google Play or App Store account settings. The renewal
    charge is applied within 24 hours before the end of the current period.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    The weekly plan includes a 3-day free trial. If you do not cancel before the trial ends, you
    will be automatically charged the price of the selected plan. Only one free trial is allowed
    per Google Play or App Store account.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Refund and cancellation policy</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Cancellation:</strong> you may cancel your subscription at any time through Google
    Play → Subscriptions → Kaxa → Cancel, or through App Store → Settings → Subscriptions.
    Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current paid period; you retain Premium access
    until that date. No prorated refunds are issued for unused time within a period.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Refunds:</strong> refunds are handled directly by Google Play or the App Store
    according to their policies. Google Play allows refund requests within the first 48 hours of
    a purchase at play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions. Kaxa does not process refunds
    directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Statutory rights:</strong> nothing in this policy limits any refund or warranty
    rights you may have under the laws of your country of residence.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Right of withdrawal (EU and UK users)</h2>
  <p>
    If you reside in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you have the right to withdraw
    from a digital services contract within 14 days of purchase (cooling-off period). However,
    by beginning to use the app within that period, you acknowledge and agree that the digital
    service has begun to be performed and that, to the extent the service has already been
    provided, you waive your right of withdrawal. Refunds for unused periods are handled through
    the corresponding app store. This clause does not affect other consumer rights recognized
    under applicable local law.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree to use Kaxa only for personal, lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to Kaxa's systems.</li>
    <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or disassemble the app.</li>
    <li>Use the app in a way that could damage, disable, or overburden the service.</li>
    <li>Use the AI feature to process information about third parties without their consent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Kaxa, its logo, design, and content are owned by its developers. No ownership rights over
    the app are granted by using the service, only a limited, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable,
    non-transferable license to use it in accordance with these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>We are not responsible for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Financial decisions made based on information recorded in the app.</li>
    <li>Interpretation or categorization errors generated by the AI feature.</li>
    <li>Losses arising from data entry errors, technical failures, or service interruptions.</li>
    <li>Data loss due to uninstallation, device reset, or hardware failure.</li>
    <li>Interruptions caused by factors outside our control (force majeure, third-party failures, etc.).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, to the maximum extent permitted
    by applicable law. This limitation does not apply where local law expressly prohibits it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to the service</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify, suspend, or discontinue features of Kaxa at any time. If a change
    significantly affects your subscription, we will try to notify you with reasonable advance
    notice through the app or by email.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Termination and data upon cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using Kaxa and cancel your subscription at any time. Upon cancellation, you
    retain Premium access until the end of the paid period. Your financial data remains on your
    device until you uninstall the app or manually delete its data. We may suspend access for
    accounts that violate these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law and dispute resolution</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Honduras, without prejudice to the
    consumer protection provisions of your country of residence that cannot be contractually
    excluded. Any dispute that cannot be resolved amicably will be submitted to the competent
    courts, respecting the procedural rights recognized in your jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about these Terms of Service, write to us at
    <a href={`mailto:${t.footer.contactEmail}`} class="text-primary underline">{t.footer.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
